From: AFK Agent <agent@agentafk.com>
Date: Thu, 08 Oct 2026 19:16:13 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 0014] add disableLigatures to TerminalView, both renderers

Three files. MacTerminalView.swift gets the backing Bool (_disableLigatures = false).
AppleTerminalView.swift gets an open property that flushes resetCaches() on change,
and injects kCTLigatureAttributeName=0 into every getAttributes dict when set.
MetalTerminalRenderer.swift extends ShaperKey with disableLigatures and threads the
flag through shape(text:font:disableLigatures:) so the CTLine is built with the same
attribute. Both caches key on the flag; a toggle hits no stale entry.
Default false — ligatures stay on, matching every other terminal's default.
---

